  "description": "Offshore Wind Technical Potential is a dataset listed in energydata.info, an open data portal for energy in developing countries under the section \"Renewable energy, Resource assessments\", published or maintained by Rachel Fox (World Bank Group). This dataset presents the technical potential for offshore wind development at the country level, split into potential for fixed and floating foundations. The files are grouped per WB regions and delivered in PDF,.SHP,.KMZ (CRS:4326) and.EXCEL format. Coverage: 55 countries in Sub-Saharan Africa, East Asia and the Pacific, Europe and Central Asia, Latin America and the Caribbean, the Middle East and North Africa, South Asia. It has 72 files in XLS, SHP ZIP, KML, PDF. The portal files it under Renewable energy, Resource assessments, Wind. The portal gives 2020 as the release date. It is reached through the links recorded on this page, with the catalogue entry as the discovery route. Access is free of charge and open. The licence is CC-BY-4.0. Caveats: this record was written from the catalogue listing only, so the linked page was not opened, its contents and current availability were not checked, and the description may lag the source. It can support power-system and electrification planning studies. Related record: the catalogue-level record data-energydata-info-world-bank.",
